# L §2.4 Expressions: "one space around binary operators and after commas, none inside brackets. Parentheses appear
# only where precedence needs them, except that a `... to u` call used as an operand and a converted flows or value
# inside a comparison (parse rule 4) are always parenthesised" (h, i, j: added or kept; a, b, c, d, e, g: the pairs
# precedence doesn't need go, x - (y - z) and (if ...) + 1 keep theirs). Numbers: "the shortest exact decimal, with a
# leading 0 before the point (0.05) and thousands grouped by a space (96 000, 1 190.05), or as a reduced a/b when the
# value doesn't terminate (round 17 settled the example: 96000.00 prints 96 000). A value of the unit % prints with it" (f, n, o, p, q; the fraction 5/900 is 1/180). L §2.1:
# units "written without spaces inside them: 8 PLN/hour", "binary minus is written with a space on each side (a - b),
# as the canonical form prints it", a span `a .. b` in an expression (m) and a version's `2026..` touching.
=== options reprint
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

def a: num = ((x + y)) * z
def b: num = x - (y - z)
def c: num = x - (y*z)
def d: num = (x * y) + z
def e: bool = not (p and q) or (r)
def f: num PLN = 1190.050 PLN+x*2
def g: num = -(x) + (- y)
def h: bool = (x to 0.01) > y
def i: num = - x to 0.01 + y
def j: bool = flows(k, 2026-01..2026-03) in PLN at fx half-up>3 PLN
def k: num PLN/hour = 8 PLN/hour*2
def l: num = sum(v[t] for t in ks where t != aa)
def m: num = flows(p , 2026-01-01..2026-03-31)
def n: rate = 19 %
def o: num = 96000.00
def p: num = 1000000.5
def q: num = 0.050
def r: num = (if c then a else b) + 1
def s: num = ?"why"
def t: bool = (x[k1 , k2].f) == (min(a,b))

version v
  cite src
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  w = 5/900
  w2 = -0.50 "art. 1"
